{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","prNumber":339,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/339","prRepository":"orin-dx/callisto","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:17:07.588Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01RnkWesCzJyeY97T2UxQPcQ","lastSequenceNum":4761,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"15d2c978-3aea-4406-ab1d-f5cd16c7b78a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c3a3639-3f25-4da0-a04d-6fa0a8c4ffa2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pukeh8f6SddnPBpcoG2rEJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/publishing.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"1b60ecec-0fa7-4f40-9b3c-62df5a76f0e4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:17:07.605Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main/docs/publishing.md","oldString":"Add this only in the protected `execute` job,","newString":"Add this only in the `execute` job,","originalFile":"# Publishing: registry authentication\n\nRegistry credential setup only. For the release lifecycle itself (local `callisto release`, generated workflows, recovery, execution semantics), see [`releasing.md`](releasing.md). For the `[registries.<name>]` config schema, see [`config.md`](config.md).\n\nCallisto delegates authentication to `cargo`, `npm`/`pnpm`, and `twine`. Configure credentials for those tools in the publishing job.\n\n---\n\n## npm\n\nTwo supported patterns.\n\n### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`\n\nSet an `NPM_TOKEN` secret. Add this only in the protected `execute` job, immediately before the publish step:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Authenticate with npm registry\n  run: npm config set //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken $NPM_TOKEN\n  env:\n    NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n\n- run: callisto release execute --intent \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-intent/release-intent.json\" --receipt \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-receipt.json\" --orchestration-revision \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n```\n\n`npm config set` writes the user-level `.npmrc` for later publish calls in the job. The version-PR action receives no token.\n\n### Pattern B: `actions/setup-node` with `registry-url`\n\n`actions/setup-node`, given `registry-url`, writes a project-level `.npmrc` that reads the token from `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`:\n\n```yaml\n- uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n  with:\n    node-version: '20'\n    registry-url: 'https://registry.npmjs.org'\n\n- run: callisto release execute --intent \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-intent/release-intent.json\" --receipt \"$RUNNER_TEMP/release-receipt.json\" --orchestration-revision \"$GITHUB_SHA\"\n  env:\n    NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n```\n\n`NODE_AUTH_TOKEN` needs an `.npmrc` entry containing `${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}`. `setup-node` writes it only when `registry-url` is set. The environment variable alone does not authenticate npm.\n\n### Choosing a pattern\n\n| Criterion | Pattern A (`NPM_TOKEN` + manual step) | Pattern B (`setup-node` + `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Depends on `actions/setup-node` | No | Yes — `registry-url` must be set |\n| Node.js version management | Separate step or pre-installed | Handled by `setup-node` |\n| Recommended when | `execute` job doesn't otherwise need Node setup | `execute` job already uses `setup-node` |\n| Release-PR action receives the token | Never | Never |\n\n### Provenance\n\nGive the `execute` job `permissions: id-token: write` and set `NPM_CONFIG_PROVENANCE: \"true\"` in its env. npm then attests each package to the workflow run and commit; Callisto needs no flag.\n\n---\n\n## Cargo (crates.io)\n\nSet `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` as a repository secret and pass it to the job environment:\n\n```yaml\nenv:\n  CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN }}\n```\n\nCargo reads this variable directly; no `.cargo/credentials` step is needed. In this repo, inject it only into `execute`.\n\n---\n\n## Python (PyPI)\n\nPublishing uses `twine upload`, which reads `TWINE_USERNAME` (`__token__` for a PyPI API token) and `TWINE_PASSWORD` (the token value):\n\n```yaml\nenv:\n  TWINE_USERNAME: __token__\n  TWINE_PASSWORD: ${{ secrets.PYPI_TOKEN }}\n```\n\nDo not use `TWINE_API_TOKEN` — twine does not recognize that variable name.\n\nThe release action maps the `PYPI_TOKEN` secret to `TWINE_USERNAME` and `TWINE_PASSWORD` itself. A workflow that runs `twine` directly must set both, because the secret name alone does not configure Twine.\n\n### Generated Callisto workflows\n\nGenerated release workflows accept `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, `NPM_TOKEN`, and `PYPI_TOKEN` as secrets. They supply each token only during publishing. Custom npm registries need their own native configuration.\n\nNative publish hooks, including `prepare` and `prepublishOnly`, run unchanged with their usual publishing environment.\n\n### Current Python support limits\n\nCallisto supports static PEP 621 or Poetry versions with `python -m build` and Twine. Current limits:\n\n- Co-located Cargo/Maturin projects fail discovery with E007, including Cargo-owned dynamic Python versions.\n- Without a sealed build, files an earlier attempt uploaded are matched by name, not by content: a rebuild is not always byte-identical. A package whose wheel name depends on the platform uploads another wheel when rerun on a different machine. A file this run uploads must match the digest the index serves for it; an index that serves no digest is accepted, because only sealed files require one. Builds set `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` to the release commit time, which makes hatchling, poetry-core, uv_build and pdm-backend wheels, and setuptools wheels, repeat byte for byte; sdists from setuptools and pdm-backend still differ.\n- A sealed build is used only by the generated build-matrix workflow, which builds in a `build-python` job without credentials and seals the files in the manifest. The generated execute job installs a pinned `twine` into a venv on its PATH; a hand-written workflow must provide `twine` itself. Sealing is opt-in at execution: a manifest that seals no Python files, or no manifest at all, builds in the executing job and warns. A sealed file the index serves without a sha256 is treated as differing. A workspace whose only release work is Python uses the single-job workflow, which installs pinned `build` and `twine` before the release step, and is not sealed. With a sealed build the run uploads exactly the built files, and a file on the index under a sealed name with different bytes stops the release (E307).\n- A release can only be completed for 14 days after its first file; after that, PyPI [refuses new files](https://blog.pypi.org/posts/2026-07-22-releases-now-reject-new-files-after-14-days/) and the release needs a new version.\n- A package tagged by an earlier version of callisto with only some of its files uploaded is reported as released when rerun at the same commit. Finish it by uploading the missing files with `twine`.\n- A configured `url` is the simple index Callisto reads and, unless `publish-url` names another endpoint, the one Twine uploads to. Private indexes with read authentication or HTML-only responses need explicit support. Twine credentials do not authenticate `curl`.\n- Dependencies in `[dependency-groups]`, Poetry groups and the legacy dev-dependency tables are not followed or rewritten when a workspace package is released. Under uv a version pin on a workspace member is ignored, and Poetry normally references siblings by path, so a stale pin there is harmless; a group that pins a registry version of a sibling is not updated.\n- `release` refuses snapshot versions (E169), so a snapshot is never published. Python snapshots use a PEP 440 local label (`0.0.0.dev0+<tag>.<sha>`), which public PyPI would reject anyway. See [PEP 440](https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/version-specifiers/).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":7,"newStart":12,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ### Pattern A: manual `.npmrc` via `NPM_TOKEN`"," ","-Set an `NPM_TOKEN` secret. Add this only in the protected `execute` job, immediately before the publish step:","+Set an `NPM_TOKEN` secret. Add this only in the `execute` job, immediately before the publish step:"," "," ```yaml"," - name: Authenticate with npm registry"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15d2c978-3aea-4406-ab1d-f5cd16c7b78a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"1b60ecec-0fa7-4f40-9b3c-62df5a76f0e4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01Pukeh8f6SddnPBpcoG2rEJ","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"smoke-main\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":40},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c6319ead-86cf-45ca-84d7-965a27987bb3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:17:07.604Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"c6319ead-86cf-45ca-84d7-965a27987bb3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Qpn1efNR6u7R4anakE5ET8","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk grep -n \\\"protected\\\" docs/*.md README.md SECURITY.md | head; sed -n 16,19p SECURITY.md; sed -n 182,186p crates/callisto-graph/src/aggregate.rs; sed -n 38,42p crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/mod.rs; sed -n 133,139p crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs; sed -n 193,199p crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/status.rs\",\"description\":\"Read remaining stale lines in SECURITY and validate-related comments\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":15},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fc42f3f9-578a-4c79-a89c-b0adfb8ff5f1","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:17:07.624Z","session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
{"parentUuid":"880dd00e-9a97-40c8-9790-ce9958e47522","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c3a3639-3f25-4da0-a04d-6fa0a8c4ffa2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qpn1efNR6u7R4anakE5ET8","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/releasing.md:67:The generated workflow keeps a release PR current. Merging that PR to the protected default branch authorizes publication; Callisto adds no approval step. Require reviews and CI checks in branch protection. A CODEOWNERS file alone does not enforce review.\nCallisto edits manifests and pushes releases across multiple package registries from inside CI, so the threat model is higher-stakes than a typical CLI tool:\n\n- **Registry token exposure** — Callisto's own release workflow (`.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml`) grants `contents`/`pull-requests` write only to the jobs that need them (`version-pr`, `execute`); registry credentials (`CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, and `NPM_TOKEN`/`TWINE_PASSWORD` for workspaces that publish npm/PyPI packages) reach only the `execute` job. A way to make Callisto, or the in-repo `.github/actions/callisto-action`, exfiltrate those tokens, or publish to a package other than the one it was asked to, is a critical finding.\n- **Workflow/action injection** — Callisto is designed to run unattended on `push` to `main` in downstream repos. An untrusted PR that could get its content executed by the release workflow (rather than merely analyzed) is in scope.\n///\n/// `Ok(None)`: no match (unknown package, reported separately by\n/// `validate`). `Ok(Some(pkg))`: unambiguous. `Err(AmbiguousName)`: two or\n/// more matches (E103).\npub(crate) fn resolve_target_package<'a>(\n///\n/// Used by `snapshot`, which must abort *before* touching any\n/// files/tags on an error diagnostic -- unlike `status`/`validate`/`version`,\n/// which fold escalated diagnostics into their report and gate on exit code\n/// instead of an `Err`.\n\n    let mut diagnostics = ws.graph.diagnostics().to_vec();\n    diagnostics.extend(tags.diagnostics.iter().cloned());\n    // Fold in every well-formedness diagnostic `validate` used to\n    // report (EmptyChangeset, UnknownPackage, AmbiguousPackageName,\n    // InvalidPackageName) now that `validate` is gone.\n    diagnostics.extend(changeset_wellformedness_diagnostics(\n    })\n}\n\n/// The per-changeset well-formedness diagnostics `validate` used to emit\n/// (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs, now removed): entries shape and\n/// package-name resolution. Resolves through the same identity index\n/// `resolve_pending_changesets` does, but this scan must never abort early,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"103a7e35-ee44-44bc-b300-85c81256680e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:17:09.560Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/releasing.md:67:The generated workflow keeps a release PR current. Merging that PR to the protected default branch authorizes publication; Callisto adds no approval step. Require reviews and CI checks in branch protection. A CODEOWNERS file alone does not enforce review.\nCallisto edits manifests and pushes releases across multiple package registries from inside CI, so the threat model is higher-stakes than a typical CLI tool:\n\n- **Registry token exposure** — Callisto's own release workflow (`.github/workflows/callisto-release.yml`) grants `contents`/`pull-requests` write only to the jobs that need them (`version-pr`, `execute`); registry credentials (`CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN`, and `NPM_TOKEN`/`TWINE_PASSWORD` for workspaces that publish npm/PyPI packages) reach only the `execute` job. A way to make Callisto, or the in-repo `.github/actions/callisto-action`, exfiltrate those tokens, or publish to a package other than the one it was asked to, is a critical finding.\n- **Workflow/action injection** — Callisto is designed to run unattended on `push` to `main` in downstream repos. An untrusted PR that could get its content executed by the release workflow (rather than merely analyzed) is in scope.\n///\n/// `Ok(None)`: no match (unknown package, reported separately by\n/// `validate`). `Ok(Some(pkg))`: unambiguous. `Err(AmbiguousName)`: two or\n/// more matches (E103).\npub(crate) fn resolve_target_package<'a>(\n///\n/// Used by `snapshot`, which must abort *before* touching any\n/// files/tags on an error diagnostic -- unlike `status`/`validate`/`version`,\n/// which fold escalated diagnostics into their report and gate on exit code\n/// instead of an `Err`.\n\n    let mut diagnostics = ws.graph.diagnostics().to_vec();\n    diagnostics.extend(tags.diagnostics.iter().cloned());\n    // Fold in every well-formedness diagnostic `validate` used to\n    // report (EmptyChangeset, UnknownPackage, AmbiguousPackageName,\n    // InvalidPackageName) now that `validate` is gone.\n    diagnostics.extend(changeset_wellformedness_diagnostics(\n    })\n}\n\n/// The per-changeset well-formedness diagnostics `validate` used to emit\n/// (crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/validate.rs, now removed): entries shape and\n/// package-name resolution. Resolves through the same identity index\n/// `resolve_pending_changesets` does, but this scan must never abort early,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4a9f2cdc-b19b-4dc8-84fc-a7869bbb5835","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","branch":"docs/cleanup-stale","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":3,"modified":22,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/callisto","visibility":"public"}]}},"