{"parentUuid":"4132806b-2105-4b9b-a8bb-8ab1ca9fe78a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c3a3639-3f25-4da0-a04d-6fa0a8c4ffa2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013MrRfyRkzVoKggAQcefivr","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 9 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: project-post-0-10-2-plan\n3\tdescription: \"Where the post-0.10.2 work plan lives (.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md, local only), what is open, and what is blocked on owner decisions.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: f98f161c-abe7-472b-92f1-8cfe1cfdf74a\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-14T17:47:05.518Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t0.10.2 published 2026-10-14 (0.10.1 was never published; its changes shipped inside 0.10.2). The plan for what comes next is `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md` (local only, git-excluded, never commit or PR it) : twelve workstreams with briefs, parallel lanes, stacked-PR order, and open owner decisions. Read it first in a fresh session, then only the contracts each brief names.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** the session that shipped 0.10.x ended with many open threads (SYS-RETRY, SYS-PYFILES/PYROUTES, SYS-BARRIER, SYS-NAPI, SYS-MATURIN, SYS-OWNER/DEMOTION, refactors R1/R3/R5, test debt, cleanup). The plan keeps context out of chat history.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** pick a lane from the plan, use one worktree per lane, stack PRs with `gh stack link`, run one `env -u FORCE_COLOR just ci` at a time. D01 (owner contract) blocks SYS-MATURIN and SYS-OWNER/DEMOTION; do not start those without the owner's decision. Delete a workstream from the file when it ships. See [[feedback-prove-with-the-real-tool]].\n16\t"}]},"uuid":"0a48faf7-cee9-47e3-a069-a41ad54a4b29","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:18:01.418Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/project_post_0_10_2_plan.md","content":"---\nname: project-post-0-10-2-plan\ndescription: \"Where the post-0.10.2 work plan lives (.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md, local only), what is open, and what is blocked on owner decisions.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: f98f161c-abe7-472b-92f1-8cfe1cfdf74a\n  modified: 2026-10-14T17:47:05.518Z\n---\n\n0.10.2 published 2026-10-14 (0.10.1 was never published; its changes shipped inside 0.10.2). The plan for what comes next is `.claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md` (local only, git-excluded, never commit or PR it) : twelve workstreams with briefs, parallel lanes, stacked-PR order, and open owner decisions. Read it first in a fresh session, then only the contracts each brief names.\n\n**Why:** the session that shipped 0.10.x ended with many open threads (SYS-RETRY, SYS-PYFILES/PYROUTES, SYS-BARRIER, SYS-NAPI, SYS-MATURIN, SYS-OWNER/DEMOTION, refactors R1/R3/R5, test debt, cleanup). The plan keeps context out of chat history.\n\n**How to apply:** pick a lane from the plan, use one worktree per lane, stack PRs with `gh stack link`, run one `env -u FORCE_COLOR just ci` at a time. D01 (owner contract) blocks SYS-MATURIN and SYS-OWNER/DEMOTION; do not start those without the owner's decision. Delete a workstream from the file when it ships. See [[feedback-prove-with-the-real-tool]].\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4132806b-2105-4b9b-a8bb-8ab1ca9fe78a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
