{"parentUuid":"82373f5a-876e-4de4-981f-ba5e4172afcb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c3a3639-3f25-4da0-a04d-6fa0a8c4ffa2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HMhBKbW3ucnzU9B4FoYm9J","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/MEMORY.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"6b375c17-543a-45f4-ae59-3717ad5e28e7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:18:16.082Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/memory/MEMORY.md","oldString":"- [Post-0.10.2 Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — Open work after the 0.10.2 release lives in .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it): 12 workstreams, parallel lanes, stacked PRs, owner decisions (D01 blocks MATURIN/OWNER).","newString":"- [Current Work Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it), rewritten 2026-10-23; older plans in .claude/plans/archive/; verify an item against code before treating it as open.","originalFile":"# Memory Index\n\n- [Post-0.10.2 Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — Open work after the 0.10.2 release lives in .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it): 12 workstreams, parallel lanes, stacked PRs, owner decisions (D01 blocks MATURIN/OWNER).\n- [Prove With the Real Tool](feedback_prove_with_the_real_tool.md) — Fake-tool tests and clean compiles hid the 0.10.1 gh credential regression; reproduce auth/release/registry paths with the real tool, test the failing case first, state what is unproven.\n- [Callisto Self-Release Incident — Durable Memory](project_release_self_hosting_incident_2026-09.md) — Claude invented and later misattributed the release approval gate, misunderstood rerun semantics, and repeatedly declared fixes before publication; records non-negotiable policy, verified failures, corrective architecture, and required incident protocol.\n- [Hardcoded Values — Proactive Search Required](feedback_hardcoded_values.md) — User repeatedly frustrated by missed hardcoded values; always include a dedicated pass in any audit or fix session.\n- [Track 0: gix WASI spike — NO-GO verdict](project_track0_wasi_verdict.md) — mmap ENOSYS in WASI blocks all gix object reads; callisto-moon exec-seam must use warpgate_pdk::exec_command.\n- [Publish Pipeline Audit — 38 bugs, fix ordering, semantic coupling map](project_publish_pipeline_audit.md) — Full adversarial audit complete; 5 P0s, 11 P1s, 15+ P2s; three root patterns; phased fix sequence with dependency order.\n- [Parallel Fixing Anti-Pattern](feedback_parallel_fixing.md) — Parallel agents for fixes fail on semantically coupled systems even across different files; use parallel for investigation only.\n- [Validate Each Fix Individually](feedback_validate_each_fix.md) — Run targeted tests after every individual fix; do not batch changes and rely solely on final CI run.\n- Architecture: ARCHITECTURE.md + docs/architecture/ (moved from .claude/semantic-model on 2026-09-25) — read before implementation work.\n- [Active Work](/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md) — Tracks B, E, F (resolve_package_config), G (callisto matrix) all shipped and passing just ci. Pipeline: canon→vector→lambda.\n- [Canon Pipeline Scope](feedback_canon_pipeline_scope.md) — Skip canon ceremony for targeted bug fixes with RED tests already written; canon auditor loops infinitely on implementation-detail prose.\n- [Workspace Audit 2026-08](project_workspace_audit_2026-08.md) — CLOSED: 8-dimension audit, all critical/high + all 31 medium/low findings re-verified fixed as of 2026-08-27.\n- [Found Code Needs Same Rigor](feedback_found_code_needs_same_rigor.md) — Committing pre-existing uncommitted code after only \"compiles + existing tests pass\" missed a zero-test-coverage regression; found/inherited code needs the same TDD/adversarial rigor as freshly-written code.\n- [Manifest Persist Track](project_manifest_persist_track.md) — Both Spec A (mutate/persist split) and Spec B (write-batching) shipped; the apply_version_plan redundant-open/persist audit finding is fully closed.\n- [Reviewer Must Actually Run Checks](feedback_reviewer_must_actually_run_checks.md) — lambda-reviewer falsely reported clippy clean once; always instruct review agents to run commands for real, not infer results.\n- [Iterate Reviews in Foreground](feedback_iterate_reviews_in_foreground.md) — Background agent notifications were unreliable across a multi-round spec/plan review loop; user called it out twice — run tight revise-review cycles in the foreground.\n- [PR #5 Release Pipeline Hardening](project_pr5_release_pipeline_hardening.md) — Fixed-group max-severity-wins config + no-compounding test, plus SPEC-005 ReleaseEntry.is_prerelease shipped end to end; all CI green.\n- [Track 7: Revwalk Bounding + Git Fixture Hermeticity Gap](project_git_fixture_hermeticity_gap.md) — nextest+global gpgsign causes ~120s hangs across ~13 test files; deferred as its own future track.\n- [Diagnose, Don't Guess, Environment Issues](feedback_diagnose_dont_guess_environment_issues.md) — User rejected an unverified guess (XProtect); always confirm root cause with a falsifiable test before reporting it.\n- [Recover Stale Agent Results After Session Interruption](feedback_recover_stale_agent_results.md) — Read the raw .output JSONL transcript directly when ListAgents/TaskOutput shows \"completed\" but the result looks like a stale mid-flight placeholder, instead of re-dispatching duplicates.\n- [Always Use Plugins](feedback_always_use_plugins.md) — Route PR/commit narration and audits through courier/ranger/etc. plugin agents by default, not freehand, even when I already have full context.\n- [Terse Comments Only](feedback_terse_comments.md) — One short line max, only for non-obvious WHY; stop writing multi-line prose comments in code/config even though CLAUDE.md already says this.\n- [Cargo Slowness Root Cause](project_cargo_slowness_target_pollution.md) — Hours-long builds were a polluted target/debug (1.7M .o files); wipe it, split-debuginfo=off, one invocation shape, no parallel builds; cold build is 31 s.\n- [No Red-Green, Lean Tokens](feedback_no_red_green_lean_tokens.md) — User dropped red-green testing and wants lean token spend; no heavy agent gating loops; CLI product tag callisto@{version} is intentional.\n- [PR #101 Hardening State](project_pr101_hardening_state.md) — 7 local unpushed commits fix the audited release-lifecycle defects; deferred structural work, unverified-on-GitHub items, and the git add -u lesson.\n- [Never Hard-Wrap Prose](feedback_never_hard_wrap_prose.md) — PR descriptions and all Markdown: one line per paragraph, never manual line breaks.\n- [Succinct Written Artifacts](feedback_succinct_written_artifacts.md) — Changesets, PR bodies, docs: short, plain, no AI slop or backstory.\n- [No Session Links](feedback_no_session_links.md) — Never put claude.ai session URLs/Claude-Session trailers in commits or PRs; public repo, private sessions.\n- [Verify Before Recommending](feedback_verify_before_recommending.md) — Check code, callers and sibling repos before presenting any recommendation; audit findings are leads, not conclusions.\n- [No Thin ADRs](feedback_no_thin_adrs.md) — ADRs only for significant decisions, with rejected options, enforcement and revisit triggers; process rules aren't ADRs.\n- [Budget: Lean Pipeline](feedback_budget_lean_pipeline.md) — weekly token budget; leanest pipeline that still catches bugs; no cleanup agents or rework the user has to review.\n- [Use gh stack](feedback_use_gh_stack.md) — stacked PRs must be native GitHub stacks (gh stack link); plain chained PRs get no CI.\n- [Agent Context Briefs](feedback_agent_context_briefs.md) — curated 2-4k token briefs, one agent per PR via SendMessage, small fixes directly; no forks of long sessions.\n- [Local Tracking, Not PRs](feedback_local_tracking_not_prs.md) — Tracking/handoff plans live in .claude/plans/ (git-excluded); never commit or PR them (PR #201 was closed for this).\n- [Worktree Guard Command Shapes](feedback_worktree_guard_commands.md) — worktree-isolated sessions refuse heredocs, compound commands and text naming git; use /usr/bin/git and scripts written with the Write tool.\n- [Check PR Overlap Before Parallel Branches](feedback_check_pr_overlap_before_parallel_branches.md) — run a pairwise merge-tree check on a PR batch, stack the overlapping ones, hold repo-wide refactors, give a merge order.\n- [Measure Value Before Building](feedback_measure_value_before_building.md) — tag hints reverted (#342): gain was noise-level; measure A/B (process counts + wall) and agree it earns its code before opening PRs.\n- [Entire Auto-Push Is Intended](feedback_entire_auto_push_intended.md) — owner wants Entire session/checkpoint pushes to the public origin; never flag or disable it.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" # Memory Index"," ","-- [Post-0.10.2 Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — Open work after the 0.10.2 release lives in .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it): 12 workstreams, parallel lanes, stacked PRs, owner decisions (D01 blocks MATURIN/OWNER).","+- [Current Work Plan](project_post_0_10_2_plan.md) — .claude/plans/NEXT-WORK.md (local only, never PR it), rewritten 2026-10-23; older plans in .claude/plans/archive/; verify an item against code before treating it as open."," - [Prove With the Real Tool](feedback_prove_with_the_real_tool.md) — Fake-tool tests and clean compiles hid the 0.10.1 gh credential regression; reproduce auth/release/registry paths with the real tool, test the failing case first, state what is unproven."," - [Callisto Self-Release Incident — Durable Memory](project_release_self_hosting_incident_2026-09.md) — Claude invented and later misattributed the release approval gate, misunderstood rerun semantics, and repeatedly declared fixes before publication; records non-negotiable policy, verified failures, corrective architecture, and required incident protocol."," - [Hardcoded Values — Proactive Search Required](feedback_hardcoded_values.md) — User repeatedly frustrated by missed hardcoded values; always include a dedicated pass in any audit or fix session."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"82373f5a-876e-4de4-981f-ba5e4172afcb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/worktrees/smoke-main","sessionId":"15c732d1-457b-4efc-91e5-664943f21b1c","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale","slug":"lexical-jingling-puppy"}
